A state machine that declares no `artifact:` has nothing to address, so the report cannot be
produced from the workdir alone: the command names the state and tells the caller to pass `--target`.
Paired with `a-machine-without-an-artifact-reports-with-a-target.txtar`.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-targetless/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-targetless
title: Targetless
summary: Machine with no declared artifact, addressed by --target.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-targetless/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  review: []

states:
  main:
    initial: reviewing
    statuses:
      reviewing:
        transitions:
          - to: reviewed
            when: the review is written
      reviewed: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-targetless/review/prompt.md --
---
summary: Review the work.
---

Review body.
-- fixtures/cwd/run/.keep --
-- cmd --
booping playbook-state fx-targetless --workdir run
-- exit --
1
-- stdout --
-- stderr --
error: state 'main' declares no `artifact:`; pass --target PATH
